[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189546894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109617#issuecomment-3189546894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109617","id":3189546894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-HJ-O","user":{"login":"Lielay9","id":40064911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDY0OTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40064911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9","html_url":"https://github.com/Lielay9","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T18:55:42Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T18:43:13Z","body":"@AxZelAnims https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/59404#issuecomment-2850395408\r\n> Now the problem with this is that.... using (0,0,0) Camera Rotation in 3D to achieve a perfect Transparency Sorting is basically pointless if the Camera is not rotated to see the Z-Axis of the objects anyway. \r\n>\r\n> So of course we will have to Rotate the Camera to look down. But looking down, the Transparency Sorting Issue happens.\r\n>\r\n> Isn't there like a way for Sprite3Ds and AnimatedSprite3Ds to follow a certain imaginary axis/position and not the current Camera/Editor View?\r\n>\r\n> This feels like a very necessary feature at least for Sprite3Ds and AnimatedSprite3Ds.\r\n\r\nIf you're still working with the project you may be interested in trying out this pr. (You can download the artifact via Checks>Artifacts)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189546894/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221322936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109617#issuecomment-3221322936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109617","id":3221322936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AAXy4","user":{"login":"Lielay9","id":40064911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDY0OTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40064911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9","html_url":"https://github.com/Lielay9","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T18:32:20Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T18:32:20Z","body":"I've battle tested the feature long enough to be certain it works as expected and enables sorting meshes in a way that is better for sprites in 2.5D games. This is the list of changes since the draft:\r\n\r\nChange names from `alpha_sort_heuristic`  to `transparency_sort_mode`. There are functions already named \"alpha sort\" that are short for \"alphabetic sorting\", and there exists a precedence for calling it \"transparency sorting\" e.g. SpriteBase3D documentation:\r\n>It can display translucent areas, but **transparency sorting** issues may be visible when multiple transparent materials are overlapping.\r\n\r\nThe custom axis sorting now uses the `AABB` support instead of center similar to orthogonal. Even more accurate heuristics exist, like sorting based on how many other AABBs the AABB is shadowed by, but at large they're rather slow (slower than doing OIT).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3221322936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3339952949","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109617#issuecomment-3339952949","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109617","id":3339952949,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7HE6M1","user":{"login":"AxZelAnims","id":149505031,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOlEBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149505031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims","html_url":"https://github.com/AxZelAnims","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/events{/privacy}","received_e