se this on PC?\r\n> \r\n> See [Testing pull requests](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/testing.html) in the contributing documentation 🙂\r\n\r\nMy mistake, I did try it back then but I took the Android Editor without realizing there was Windows Editor. Artifacts is now expired. \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3922698101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4374514309","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109617#issuecomment-4374514309","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109617","id":4374514309,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBL3KhQ","user":{"login":"AxZelAnims","id":149505031,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOlEBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149505031?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims","html_url":"https://github.com/AxZelAnims","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AxZelAnims/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T21:11:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T21:11:33Z","body":"Hello, I tried my very first compile, and I might have broke something during compilation (tinkered with scons having issues the entire night) as the screen now has static effect. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04edfa9c-dafe-4c6d-8d63-3e7bdfb80b9f\r\n\r\nIt works properly for sorting Transparency in 2.5D Games. The option to use it in project setting is also very useful because it affects the editor as well, not just on camera preview. \r\n\r\nSure hope this gets to be implemented officially somehow. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4374514309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5243151471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109617#issuecomment-5243151471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109617","id":5243151471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOIQkbw","user":{"login":"neikeq","id":7718100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTgxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7718100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq","html_url":"https://github.com/neikeq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T16:38:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T16:38:52Z","body":"While this does not go as far as #59404 by not introducing a stacked sorting offset (which would be ideal for many 2D in 3D games), it makes it much easier to apply workarounds that achieve a similar result, and unlike my PR it's done in a non-controversial (and correct, for the subset that this PR implements) way.\nI hope this gets eventually merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5243151471/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]